{"step_index":3449,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-29T09:40:52Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-29T05:40:52-04:00\nCompleted At: 2026-09-29T05:40:52-04:00\nFile Path: `file:///Users/ajoxendine68/Desktop/SSOT_Agentic_Brain/ops/scripts/agent_speak.sh`\nTotal Lines: 86\nTotal Bytes: 1922\nShowing lines 60 to 86\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n60: # Pure Bash File Mutex Lock & Native macOS Speech Execution\n61: LOCKDIR=\"/tmp/coreaudio_single_speaker.lockdir\"\n62: \n63: # Stale lock cleanup (if lock is older than 5 seconds)\n64: if [[ -d \"$LOCKDIR\" ]]; then\n65:   NOW_SEC=$(date +%s)\n66:   MOD_SEC=$(stat -f %m \"$LOCKDIR\" 2>/dev/null || echo 0)\n67:   LOCK_AGE=$((NOW_SEC - MOD_SEC))\n68:   if [ \"$LOCK_AGE\" -gt 5 ]; then\n69:     rm -rf \"$LOCKDIR\" 2>/dev/null || true\n70:   fi\n71: fi\n72: \n73: while ! mkdir \"$LOCKDIR\" 2>/dev/null; do\n74:   sleep 0.05\n75: done\n76: \n77: # Ensure lock cleanup on exit or error\n78: trap 'rm -rf \"$LOCKDIR\"' EXIT INT TERM\n79: \n80: # Direct Bare-Metal Audio Playback (Synchronous real-time audio output)\n81: CLEAN_TEXT=\"$(echo \"$RAW_TEXT\" | tr -d '\"')\"\n82: say -v \"$VOICE\" \"$CLEAN_TEXT\"\n83: \n84: # Update Dead Man Switch timestamp receipt\n85: date +%s > /tmp/xoras_last_speech_timestamp.txt\n86: \nThe above content does NOT show the entire file contents. If you need to view any lines of the file which were not shown to complete your task, call this tool again to view those lines.\n"}
